    "source_message_id": 742,
    "speaker": "client",
    "text": "Whether both purchase scenarios share the same modal determines the copy. If they do, the &#39;Mint successful&#39; message will need to be more generic; otherwise, a referral-code purchase will need different copy.\n\nFor purchases without a code, the current message works nicely because it reminds buyers that simply holding the NFT could one day result in receiving a random ticket and commission too. That reminder only makes sense for mints without a referral code.\n\nSeparately, the book title looks good in small caps."
